{
  "id": 465788238,
  "iid": 23992,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "Packet: Add option to disable heuristic for all protocols",
  "description": "I was trying to create a profile optimized for a single task, decoding just some protocols, and noticed that (in my use case) Wireshark spent 40% of the time in `dissector_try_heuristic` while loading files.\n\nMy idea was to introduce a preference that completely disables the heuristic for all protocols. I'm not sure if some dissectors rely on `dissector_try_heuristic` and may have some issues with this. I also noticed that some protocols have a \"Use heuristic sub-dissectors\" preference, and that may confuse the user, since the protocol-specific preference doesn't override the general one.\n\nThis were my results loading a file taken as example. Take note that it was just one measurement taken on one file. Results may vary a lot.\n\n<table>\n  <tr>\n    <th></th>\n    <th>Heuristic on</th>\n    <th>Heuristic off</th>\n    <th>Improvement</th>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <th>Default profile¹</th>\n    <td>55.638 s</td>\n    <td>29.514 s</td>\n    <td>46.95 %</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <th>Specific profile²</th>\n    <td>65.790 s</td>\n    <td>58.574 s</td>\n    <td>10.97 %</td>\n  </tr>\n</table>\n\n\n¹ Default Wireshark profile with nothing specific configured.\n\n² Profile specific for my use case, configured to decode some protocols on specific ports.",
