        {
          "id": 3184924598,
          "type": null,
          "body": "> I also noticed that some protocols have a \"Use heuristic sub-dissectors\" preference,\n\nThis should be a \"Try heuristic sub-dissectors first\" preference in most (all?) cases. It handles cases where an assigned port (or IP protocol, or whatever) gets used by something else other than the assigned protocol.\n\nI believe that many years ago individual \"turn on heuristics\" was turned off.",
